{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>From wine and strong drink.</b> As the Targum renders: ״מֵחֲמַר חֲדַת וְעַתִּיק״ — for wine intoxicates when it is old." "<b>And anything steeped.</b> A term of steeping in water and any liquid; and in the language of the Mishnah there are many: ״אֵין שׁוֹרִין דְּיוֹ וְסַמָּנִים״ (Shabbat 17), ״נָזִיר שֶׁשָּׁרָה פִּתּוֹ״ (Nazir 34)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:09:38.209894780Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}